INT. STRIKE ZONE LANES - LANE 14 - NIGHT

The neon pins glow pink over a pile of cash on the scoring table. Six people stand frozen under the haze of cigarette smoke.

KAZIMIERZ "SPUD" NOWAK, 50s, shoes untied, grips a ball like a grenade. LORETTA VANCE, 40s, red lipstick, holds the money. DUTCH AMARI, 30s, tall, leans on the ball return. PEARL, 60s, the lane attendant, polishes a shoe with great calm. GIDEON, 20s, nervously jingles car keys. MINNOW, 12, drops under the table.

SPUD
Loretta, put the cash down and nobody gets scuffed.

LORETTA
Scuffed? Spud, you rented these shoes.

DUTCH
Pearl, whose side are you on?

PEARL
Lane 14's.

Gideon bolts. Spud hurls the ball; it thunders down the lane and scatters the pins, and Gideon, mid-stride, hops and screams as his keys skid into the gutter.

MINNOW
(from under the table)
Strike!
